{% comment %}
  Availability badge — two states (see docs/SHORTLIST-PLAN.md §2.3).

  The ships:YYYY-MM-DD tag is the DATE SOURCE only, never a state switch:
  every range instrument carries one permanently (it's also readable from
  /products/{handle}.js for the JS-rendered cards, which a metafield is not).
  · ships date in the future  → "Made for you — ships 1 December 2026"
  · otherwise, stock on hand  → "In stock — ships in 1–2 working days"
  When a batch lands the date passes and the badge flips itself — no admin
  action. Range instruments use inventory policy `continue` so they never go
  unavailable; the gap between selling out and entering the next batch shows
  "in production". A sold-out one-off (`one-off` tag, policy `deny`) is hidden
  from grids/search and only renders its "Sold out" badge on a direct link.

  Usage: {% render 'availability-badge', product: product %}
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign ship_date = blank
  for t in product.tags
    if t contains 'ships:'
      assign ship_date = t | remove: 'ships:'
    endif
  endfor
  assign now_s = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
  assign ship_s = -1
  if ship_date != blank
    assign ship_s = ship_date | date: '%s' | plus: 0
  endif
  assign variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant | default: product.variants.first
-%}
{%- if ship_s > now_s -%}
  <span class="badge badge-order">Made for you. Ships {{ ship_date | date: '%-d %B %Y' }}</span>
{%- elsif product.available == false -%}
  <span class="badge badge-soldout">Sold out</span>
{%- elsif variant.inventory_management == blank or variant.inventory_quantity > 0 -%}
  <span class="badge badge-stock">In stock. Ships in 1–2 working days</span>
{%- else -%}
  <span class="badge badge-order">Made for you. In production</span>
{%- endif -%}
